A1. This is always blowing about Florida. ~ HURRICANE
A9. This is always bringing up something disagreeable. ~ NAUSEA
A11. These have caused many tears. ~ ONIONS
A14. To egg on (not on toast). ~ URGE
A15. An English song producer. ~ LINNET
A16. This is what a kid brother does when he wants to put the bawl over. ~ CRIES
A17. The kind of a friend a Scotchman makes. ~ CLOSE
A19. The Scotch used to get a pass on this. ~ BAR
A21. A donkey. ~ ASS
A22. A field Paddock. ~ HARE
A23. The kind of a trick he won with a diamond. ~ CUTE
A24. What the observing man will do. ~ SEE
A25. This is what became of Little Bo-Peep's sheep. ~ STEWS
A27. Sometimes these come to a bad end. ~ TALES
A28. These are the letters Tom Sawyer wrote. ~ TS
A29. This has created a lot of interest in financial circles. ~ LOAN
A30. This is what aviators hear when their wives go up in the air. ~ TIRADE
A31. This one helped to carry the bag for Santa Claus. ~ POSTMASTER
A33. Men who are mechanically inclined. ~ ROBOTS
A36. The kind of conversations they now have in the movies. ~ ORAL
A37. Some of these are imported from France and others come from the Chicago stock-yards. ~ ODORS
A38. This is what the loser did. ~ SWORE
A39. Nothing to speak about. ~ NIL
A41. When the boss went away he left this kind of an office force. ~ IDLE
A42. These make good drawing cards. ~ ACES
A43. This is better than nothing. ~ ONE
A44. The one who did this came out ahead. ~ LED
A45. The way she looked on the 18th day. ~ SPARE
A46. The white-haired boy. ~ BLOND
A48. You never can tell how these are going to end. ~ SERIALS
A50. It has always been our secret ambition to live in this. ~ EASE
A51. Don't let anyone hypnotize you into this. ~ TRANCE
A52. This lad ran for Notre Dame and arrived on the football field. ~ ELDER
A53. Watchfully. ~ HEEDFULLY

D1. The kind of a man that has broad views. ~ HUGE
D2. Employments. ~ USES
D3. This part of the rent will have to be put down first. ~ RE
D4. The god that gave Cleopatra her beautiful dark skin. ~ RA
D5. This is what a shy young man does to the roots of his hair. ~ COLORS
D6. A plant cultivated for its aromatic seed. ~ ANISE
D7. The number on one side of a diamond. ~ NINE
D8. The age of the universe. ~ EON
D9. The only attractive thing about a hospital (plu.). ~ NURSES
D10. It may be necessary to do this if you want to get up in the world. ~ ARISE
D12. This has something to do with the stars. (Consult Einstein and not Ziegfeld.) ~ NEBULAR
D13. Narrated. ~ STATED
D16. This is being forced down the throats of the younger generation (two words). ~ CASTOROIL
D17. To double-cross. ~ CHEAT
D18. A grasschopper (two words). ~ LAWNMOWERS
D20. This is what the twins did to each other. ~ RESEMBLED
D23. A good thing to take when you cross the street. ~ CARE
D25. Much money has been lost in these. ~ SLOTS
D26. To throw up. ~ TOSS
D27. This makes a good headliner. ~ TITLE
D30. The last Nick in a royal line. ~ TSAR
D31. A small opening. ~ PORE
D32. This is what the early Americans did at sunrise. ~ AROSE
D34. This is most extraordinary. ~ ODDEST
D35. What gangsters are becoming in Chicago. ~ BOLDER
D38. Ascended. ~ SCALED
D39. What the well-dressed killer will wear. ~ NOOSE
D40. This is the part the interior decorator decorates. ~ INNER
D42. Hastily. ~ APACE
D45. A term in mathematics. ~ SINE
D46. This one has an appealing tongue. ~ BELL
D47. This is what a flapper is apt to become according to the present styles. ~ LADY
D49. A cheering word. ~ RAH
D52. Try this if you want to travel in the upper circles. ~ EL


